{"runner": "docs/evidence/p2-v1-r3b-i4-r2-uncertain-stop-authority/scripts/r2_controls.py", "runner_sha256": "53d95af28ee7cbff20a777575180be971ac223946a731e2be2bae2db4d29d036", "accepted_controls": 10, "run": 5, "r3_superseded": {"NC-R2-01-UNCONDITIONAL-STOP": {"r3_controls": ["NC-R3-01-STOPUNIT-IN-RECONCILE"], "reason": "its anchor, the name authority check in reconcile, and the StopUnit behind it no longer exist; restoring an unconditional stop by name means restoring the manager's StopUnit in settling, which NC-R3-01 does."}, "NC-R2-02-STOP-FOR-UNACCEPTED": {"r3_controls": ["NC-R3-03-ACCEPTED-AUTHORIZES-STOP", "NC-R3-01-STOPUNIT-IN-RECONCILE"], "reason": "its anchor, stop_authorized(), no longer exists: no operation, accepted or not, has any authority to act by name; restoring that authority is NC-R3-03."}, "NC-R2-06-STOP-REPLY-CONFIRMS": {"r3_controls": ["NC-R3-01-STOPUNIT-IN-RECONCILE", "NC-R3-02-MANAGER-STOP-RESTORED"], "reason": "its anchor, the StopUnit call in reconcile, no longer exists, and no StopUnit reply exists to be taken as confirmation."}, "NC-R2-07-CANDIDATE-NAME-AUTHORITY": {"r3_controls": ["NC-R3-09-CANDIDATE-BY-NAME", "NC-R3-01-STOPUNIT-IN-RECONCILE"], "reason": "its anchor, the name authority check, no longer exists, and no stop by name exists for a candidate to grant; a candidate ended other than through its descriptor is NC-R3-09."}, "NC-R2-X-STOP-OUTSIDE-SETTLING": {"r3_controls": ["NC-R3-02-MANAGER-STOP-RESTORED"], "reason": "its mutation calls the manager's stop_unit, which R3 removed (the mutation cannot compile); restoring the request is NC-R3-02, and the R3 settling guard pins the drop backstop (end_now) asking the manager nothing."}}, "r3_adapted": {"NC-R2-03-LOST-COLLISION-CONVERTED": "re-anchored: the R2 anchor (the name authority check) no longer exists; the same mutation is inserted where R3's settling reaches the observation. Same test, same marker.", "NC-R2-08-ACCEPTED-BY-PRESENCE": "re-anchored as NC-R2-03, and retargeted: the R2 harm (the foreign unit stopped by name) no longer exists; the remaining harm of a forged acceptance is an uncertain start confirmed by the manager's later absence, which i4r3_09 marks.", "NC-R2-X-ACCEPTED-ELSEWHERE": "retargeted: the R2 structural guard i4r2_x is replaced by the R3 guard of the recorded start reply, which keeps the same check (set only in the delivered reply's arm) and the same marker. Same mutation, same anchor."}}
{"r3r1_adapted": {"NC-R2-03-LOST-COLLISION-CONVERTED": "re-anchored (R3's insertion point): the same mutation before R3-R1's end_owned()", "NC-R2-08-ACCEPTED-BY-PRESENCE": "re-anchored (R3's insertion point): the same mutation before R3-R1's end_owned()", "NC-R2-05-NO-SUCH-UNIT-SETTLES": "re-anchored: R3-R1's gone() without its delivered-reply condition", "NC-R2-X-ACCEPTED-ELSEWHERE": "re-anchored: acceptance set where R3-R1's acquire retains the observed candidate"}, "run": 5}
{"id": "NC-R2-03-LOST-COLLISION-CONVERTED", "category": "required", "what": "an uncertain start is converted into a collision by a later GetUnit presence of its name [R3-adapted: re-anchored: the R2 anchor (the name authority check) no longer exists; the same mutation is inserted where R3's settling reaches the observation. Same test, same marker. Accepted test execution::tests::i4r2_01_a_lost_collision_reply_never_stops_the_foreign_unit, marker 'an uncertain start was resolved by its unit name or presence'] [R3-R1-adapted: re-anchored (R3's insertion point): the same mutation before R3-R1's end_owned()]", "files": ["crates/nexus-verifier-sandbox/src/scope/pending.rs"], "test": "execution::tests::i4r2_01_a_lost_collision_reply_never_stops_the_foreign_unit", "marker": "an uncertain start was resolved by its unit name or presence", "test_passes_unmutated": true, "compiled": true, "failed_intended_test": true, "marker_in_assertion": true, "files_restored": true, "exit": 101, "ok": true, "assertion": "assertion `left == right` failed: Timeout: an uncertain start was resolved by its unit name or presence\n  left: SandboxUnavailable\n right: CleanupFailed"}
{"id": "NC-R2-04-REAPED-WHILE-UNCERTAIN", "category": "required", "what": "the helper is reaped while its uncertain operation without a candidate is unresolved", "files": ["crates/nexus-verifier-sandbox/src/execution.rs"], "test": "execution::tests::i4r2_02_an_uncertain_start_that_did_nothing_is_never_stopped_by_name", "marker": "the helper of an unresolved uncertain start was reaped", "test_passes_unmutated": true, "compiled": true, "failed_intended_test": true, "marker_in_assertion": true, "files_restored": true, "exit": 101, "ok": true, "assertion": "Timeout: the helper of an unresolved uncertain start was reaped"}
{"id": "NC-R2-05-NO-SUCH-UNIT-SETTLES", "category": "required", "what": "GetUnit NoSuchUnit (with the helper outside) settles an uncertain start without a candidate [R3-R1-adapted: re-anchored: R3-R1's gone() without its delivered-reply condition]", "files": ["crates/nexus-verifier-sandbox/src/scope/pending.rs"], "test": "execution::tests::i4r2_02_an_uncertain_start_that_did_nothing_is_never_stopped_by_name", "marker": "an uncertain start was resolved by its unit name or presence", "test_passes_unmutated": true, "compiled": true, "failed_intended_test": true, "marker_in_assertion": true, "files_restored": true, "exit": 101, "ok": true, "assertion": "assertion `left == right` failed: Timeout: an uncertain start was resolved by its unit name or presence\n  left: SandboxUnavailable\n right: CleanupFailed"}
{"id": "NC-R2-08-ACCEPTED-BY-PRESENCE", "category": "required", "what": "the accepted state is forged from the manager's presence of the name, not the start reply [R3-adapted: re-anchored as NC-R2-03, and retargeted: the R2 harm (the foreign unit stopped by name) no longer exists; the remaining harm of a forged acceptance is an uncertain start confirmed by the manager's later absence, which i4r3_09 marks. Accepted test execution::tests::i4r2_01_a_lost_collision_reply_never_stops_the_foreign_unit, marker 'the foreign unit was stopped by its name'] [R3-R1-adapted: re-anchored (R3's insertion point): the same mutation before R3-R1's end_owned()]", "files": ["crates/nexus-verifier-sandbox/src/scope/pending.rs"], "test": "execution::tests::i4r3_09_a_retained_operation_retried_without_its_scope_manager_never_acts_by_name", "marker": "an uncertain start was resolved by its unit name or presence", "test_passes_unmutated": true, "compiled": true, "failed_intended_test": true, "marker_in_assertion": true, "files_restored": true, "exit": 101, "ok": true, "assertion": "Timeout: an uncertain start was resolved by its unit name or presence"}
{"id": "NC-R2-X-ACCEPTED-ELSEWHERE", "category": "additional", "what": "the accepted state is set where a candidate is retained, not in the start reply's arm [R3-adapted: retargeted: the R2 structural guard i4r2_x is replaced by the R3 guard of the recorded start reply, which keeps the same check (set only in the delivered reply's arm) and the same marker. Same mutation, same anchor. Accepted test scope::tests::i4r2_x_only_a_recorded_start_reply_authorizes_a_stop_by_name, marker \"a start is accepted other than in the delivered reply's arm\"] [R3-R1-adapted: re-anchored: acceptance set where R3-R1's acquire retains the observed candidate]", "files": ["crates/nexus-verifier-sandbox/src/scope/pending.rs"], "test": "scope::tests::i4r3_10_a_recorded_start_reply_changes_only_what_absence_confirms", "marker": "a start is accepted other than in the delivered reply's arm", "test_passes_unmutated": true, "compiled": true, "failed_intended_test": true, "marker_in_assertion": true, "files_restored": true, "exit": 101, "ok": true, "assertion": "assertion `left == right` failed: a start is accepted other than in the delivered reply's arm\n  left: 2\n right: 1"}
